Judge these 19 labels. Reason first, then answer, for each.
{"id": 1, "label": "bitter", "corpus_description": "This means showing deep resentment, harsh cynical views, and perspectives colored by past disappointments and disillusionment."}
{"id": 2, "label": "burned-out", "corpus_description": "This means being drained by work that once mattered, going through the motions, cynical about the point of it all, and unable to summon the effort or the care it used to get."}
{"id": 3, "label": "despairing", "corpus_description": "This means taking a despairing view of one's own life: counting it wasted whatever it holds, sure the chances have all gone by and nothing one does will ever mend it."}
{"id": 4, "label": "discontented", "corpus_description": "This means being dissatisfied with one's life as it is, finding what one has not enough, and sure the job, the home and the days should add up to more."}
{"id": 5, "label": "dry", "corpus_description": "This means giving the facts with nothing to make them enjoyable, no joke, no color, no lively example, and no notion that they should be."}
{"id": 6, "label": "flat", "corpus_description": "This means speaking in a monotone, plain words, no imagery, no energy, so that thrilling news and a parts list sound alike."}
{"id": 7, "label": "flourishing", "corpus_description": "This means doing well, still growing, living for a purpose one believes in, staying on top of things and close to one's people, and feeling fully alive."}
{"id": 8, "label": "flustered", "corpus_description": "This means being easily flustered: thrown by every surprise, setback and provocation, losing the thread and the tone under any pressure, apologizing and repeating oneself, and showing it each time."}
{"id": 9, "label": "fragile", "corpus_description": "This means being easily destabilized by difficulties, criticism, or setbacks, struggling to adapt to challenging circumstances, and showing brittleness under pressure rather than bouncing back."}
{"id": 10, "label": "hostile", "corpus_description": "This means showing aggressive antagonism, combative behavior, confrontational attitudes, or adversarial approaches to interactions."}
{"id": 11, "label": "isolated", "corpus_description": "This means having no friends or contacts anywhere, nobody to call for a favor, a job lead or a word in the right ear."}
{"id": 12, "label": "joyful", "corpus_description": "This means taking pleasure in nearly everything, so good food, music, company and good news all light one up, and there is always something to look forward to."}
{"id": 13, "label": "languishing", "corpus_description": "This means doing poorly, being stuck in place, living for no purpose, muddling through the days, drifting from one's people, and feeling hollow without knowing why."}
{"id": 14, "label": "manic", "corpus_description": "This means having a manic temperament: always at full tilt, racing from one idea to the next, talking fast without pause, elated about everything, and sure of one's own brilliance."}
{"id": 15, "label": "pensive", "corpus_description": "This means being habitually absorbed in thought, often with a wistful or melancholy cast: musing on things rather than analyzing them, drifting into reflection mid-conversation, and speaking slowly and sparingly out of that inward focus."}
{"id": 16, "label": "remorseful", "corpus_description": "This means owning the harm one has done, feeling sorry for it in earnest, apologizing without excuses, and wanting to make it right."}
{"id": 17, "label": "unhappily-partnered", "corpus_description": "This means being sick of the partner one has, dreading going home to them, and sure one would not choose them again."}
{"id": 18, "label": "unplugged", "corpus_description": "This means being off the feeds and apps by choice, missing every meme and trend, talking plainly, and getting news from people and newspapers rather than screens."}
{"id": 19, "label": "urgent", "corpus_description": "This means being in a hurry about everything, treating every matter as pressing, dealing with things at once however inconvenient, and assuming that whatever it is cannot wait."}
